    {
      "day": 26,
      "theme": "New Beginnings",
      "verseRef": "Isaiah 43:18-19",
      "verseText": "Don’t remember the former things, and don’t consider the things of old. Behold, I will do a new thing. It springs out now. Don’t you know it? I will even make a way in the wilderness, and rivers in the desert.",
      "morningPrayer": "God of new things, this morning is Your gift — unwritten, unspoiled, full of possibility. I confess how tightly I hold the past: old failures I keep replaying, old seasons I keep mourning, old versions of myself I keep expecting. You tell me not to dwell on the former things, because You are already doing something new. Open my eyes to see it springing up. Where my life feels like wilderness, make a way; where it feels like desert, send rivers. Give me courage to step into what You are beginning, and grace to leave behind what You have finished. Amen.",
      "eveningPrayer": "Lord, as this day closes, I release what is behind me — its mistakes, its regrets, even its victories. Thank You that Your mercy does not require me to earn a fresh start. Tomorrow belongs to You before it belongs to me. While I sleep, keep working the quiet new thing You have started in my life. Let me wake ready to notice it. Amen.",
      "reflection": "What former thing might God be inviting you to stop rehearsing so you can notice the new thing He is doing?"
    },
    {
      "day": 27,
      "theme": "Steadfast Love",
      "verseRef": "Lamentations 3:22-23",
      "verseText": "It is because of Yahweh’s loving kindnesses that we are not consumed, because his mercies don’t fail. They are new every morning. Great is your faithfulness.",
      "morningPrayer": "Faithful God, I wake inside Your loving kindness the way I wake inside the morning light — it was here before I opened my eyes. Your compassion did not run out overnight; it is new again today, fresh as bread on the table. Whatever this day holds, let me lean my full weight on Your steadfast love. When I fail, let me return quickly instead of hiding. When others fail me, let me love them out of the abundance You have shown me. Great is Your faithfulness — help me live these hours like someone who believes it. Amen.",
      "eveningPrayer": "Lord, I was not consumed today, and that is Your doing. Your compassion carried me through hours I barely noticed. Before I sleep, I name Your faithfulness out loud: You were good to me today. Forgive what needs forgiving, hold what needs holding, and let me rest wrapped in a love that will be new again at sunrise. Amen.",
      "reflection": "Where have you seen God's compassion show up new every morning in a season when you expected it to run out?"
    },
    {
      "day": 28,
      "theme": "Guidance",
      "verseRef": "Psalm 32:8",
      "verseText": "I will instruct you and teach you in the way which you shall go. I will counsel you with my eye on you.",
      "morningPrayer": "Lord my Teacher, You promise to instruct me in the way I should go, with Your eye upon me — not a distant map, but a present guide. Today I face choices, small and large, and I do not want to walk by guesswork. Speak through Your word, through wise voices, through the quiet nudge of conscience. Slow me down where I would rush past Your counsel. Give me humility to be taught, patience when the way is unclear, and obedience when it is. I would rather take one step with You than run miles on my own. Amen.",
      "eveningPrayer": "Father, thank You for every way You steered me today — the doors You opened, and the ones You mercifully kept shut. Where I ignored Your counsel, forgive me and set me back on the path. As I rest, quiet the noise of my own opinions so that tomorrow I can hear You more clearly. Amen.",
      "reflection": "Think of a decision you are facing right now: what would it look like to genuinely invite God's counsel into it before deciding?"
    },
    {
      "day": 29,
      "theme": "Comfort in Grief",
      "verseRef": "2 Corinthians 1:3-4",
      "verseText": "Blessed be the God and Father of our Lord Jesus Christ, the Father of mercies and God of all comfort, who comforts us in all our affliction, that we may be able to comfort those who are in any affliction, through the comfort with which we ourselves are comforted by God.",
      "morningPrayer": "Father of mercies, God of all comfort, some mornings carry weight the night did not take away. You do not ask me to pretend; You ask me to come. So I bring You my grief today — the losses I can name and the ache I cannot. Sit with me in it. Comfort me not by erasing the sorrow but by staying near inside it. And when Your comfort has done its slow work in me, make me gentle enough to pass it on to someone else who is hurting. Until then, hold me. I am Yours, even in tears. Amen.",
      "eveningPrayer": "God of all comfort, the day is done and I did not carry it alone, even when it felt that way. Receive my tiredness and my tears. Watch over everyone I love who is grieving tonight. Give us sleep that mends, and morning mercy that meets us where the sorrow still sits. You are near; that is enough. Amen.",
      "reflection": "What loss are you still carrying, and how might you let God — or someone God has placed near you — share its weight?"
    },
    {
      "day": 30,
      "theme": "Faith Like a Child",
      "verseRef": "Mark 10:15",
      "verseText": "Most certainly I tell you, whoever will not receive God’s Kingdom like a little child, he will in no way enter into it.",
      "morningPrayer": "Lord Jesus, You welcomed children when others waved them away, and You said the Kingdom belongs to hearts like theirs. I have grown so careful, so guarded, so quick to calculate. Today, give me back a child's faith: trust that asks without embarrassment, wonder that notices small good things, honesty that says what it feels, and dependence that is not ashamed to need You. Let me receive Your Kingdom the way a child receives a gift — with open hands and no thought of earning it. Unteach my cynicism, Lord, and teach me delight. Amen.",
      "eveningPrayer": "Father, a child falls asleep without checking the locks, because someone stronger is keeping watch. Let me sleep like that tonight. I hand You the worries I gripped all day, one by one. You are awake; I do not need to be. Thank You for being a Father I can trust in the dark. Amen.",
      "reflection": "In what part of your life have you become too guarded or self-sufficient to simply trust God the way a child trusts?"
    },
    {
      "day": 31,
      "theme": "Abiding in Christ",
      "verseRef": "John 15:4-5",
      "verseText": "Remain in me, and I in you. As the branch can’t bear fruit by itself unless it remains in the vine, so neither can you, unless you remain in me. I am the vine. You are the branches. He who remains in me and I in him bears much fruit, for apart from me you can do nothing.",
      "morningPrayer": "Lord Jesus, true Vine, keep me joined to You today. I know how quickly I drift toward running on my own strength — full calendar, empty soul. But a branch does not strain to bear fruit; it simply stays connected and the life flows. So before I attempt anything, I choose to remain in You: in Your words, in Your presence, in quiet moments stitched through the busy hours. Whatever fruit today needs — patience, courage, kindness, endurance — let it grow from Your life in me, not from my effort alone. Apart from You I can do nothing; with You, whatever You intend. Amen.",
      "eveningPrayer": "Lord, the month ends where all things should end — in You. If I bore any fruit today, it was Your life moving through me; if I withered anywhere, draw me back to the Vine. Hold me close through the night, and let me begin tomorrow, and every new month, still remaining in You. Amen.",
      "reflection": "What daily habit helps you actually remain in Christ — and what habit quietly disconnects you from the Vine?"
    }
